** DISCOVERY WHEN IM OUTSIDE THE NETWORK **

Discovery using ICMP:
 fping -g 192.168.1.0/24 -> scans full network to find active ips (using ICMP)
 nmap -PE -PM -PP -sn -n 199.66.11.0/24 -> Send echo, timestamp requests and subnet mask requests

Discovery using TCP ports:
 masscan -p20,21-23,25,53,80,110,111,135,139,143,443,445,993,995,1723,3306,3389,5900,8080 199.66.11.0/24

HTTP discovery:
 masscan -p80,443,8000-8100,8443 199.66.11.0/24

UDP discovery: 
 nmap -sU -sV --version-intensity 0 -F -n 199.66.11.53/24
 # The -sV will make nmap test each possible known UDP service packet
 # The "--version-intensity 0" will make nmap only test the most probable
 ## for faster result use udp-proto-scanner "github" // example: ./udp-proto-scanner 192.168.1.17/24

SCTP discovery scan:
 nmap -T4 -sY -n --open -Pn <IP/range> # this is used by telecommunication (4G / 5G) and its not widely used 
 # more info: SCTP is called TCPng ( next-generation ) 

Useful to grep only active ip addresses:
 nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24 -oG - | grep "Up" | awk '{print $2}'


** DISCOVERY WHEN IM INSIDE THE NETWORK **

Passive discovery (stealth): 
 netdiscover -p (nmap but passive & slower)
 p0f -i eth0 -p -o /tmp/p0f.log # capture communication passively only when authorized (you need router level to capture all the connections)
 
 # Bettercap
 net.recon on/off #Read local ARP cache periodically
 net.show
 set net.show.meta true #more info


Active discovery:
 #ARP discovery
 nmap -sn <Network>       #ARP Requests (Discover IPs)
 netdiscover -r <Network> #ARP requests (Discover IPs) only if nmap is flagged or blocked

 #NBT discovery
 nbtscan -r 192.168.0.1/24 #Search in Domain (on windows systems)

 # Bettercap (when MiTM)
 net.probe on/off               #Discover hosts on current subnet by probing with ARP, mDNS, NBNS, UPNP, and/or WSD
 set net.probe.mdns true/false  #Enable mDNS discovery probes (default=true)
 set net.probe.nbns true/false  #Enable NetBIOS name service discovery probes (default=true)
 set net.probe.upnp true/false  #Enable UPNP discovery probes (default=true)
 set net.probe.wsd true/false   #Enable WSD discovery probes (default=true)
 set net.probe.throttle 10      #10ms between probes sent (default=10)

 #IPv6
 alive6 <IFACE> # Send a pingv6 to multicast. (rare)
 
Active ICMP:
 ip neigh                # show all neighbors
 ping -b 255.255.255.255 => Limited broadcast: sends to all hosts on the local network segment (generic LAN broadcast)
 ping -b 192.168.1.255   => Directed broadcast: sends to all hosts specifically in the 192.168.1.0/24 subnet


** HOST SCANNING **
 # Nmap fast scan for the most 1000tcp ports used
 nmap -sV -sC -O -T4 -n -Pn -oA fastscan <IP>
 # Nmap fast scan for all the ports
 nmap -sV -sC -O -T4 -n -Pn -p- -oA fullfastscan <IP>
 # Nmap fast scan for all the ports slower to avoid failures due to -T4
 nmap -sV -sC -O -p- -n -Pn -oA fullscan <IP>
 NOTE:
   * Service version detection (-sV)
   * OS detection (-O)
   * Script scanning (-sC)
   * Better output formats (-oA)  

